01:09:55.429 --> 01:09:56.558
- Yeah, and also back then,

01:09:56.558 --> 01:09:58.287
I feel like you just had a lot less choice

01:09:58.287 --> 01:09:59.721
of what games you could play, you know.

01:09:59.721 --> 01:10:00.972
As a kid, I'm just like, yeah,

01:10:00.972 --> 01:10:04.217
I waited for fucking five
months for the new Mario game

01:10:04.217 --> 01:10:06.137
'cause there was nothing
else to look forward to.

01:10:06.137 --> 01:10:07.597
There's literally nothing
to fill that void.

01:10:07.597 --> 01:10:12.233
I couldn't get a free to play
game like Genshin. (laughs)

01:10:12.233 --> 01:10:13.493
- Free to play game, that's just-

01:10:13.493 --> 01:10:14.326
- It's free to play? (laughs)

01:10:14.326 --> 01:10:15.762
- Like "Fortnite" or "League of Legends"

01:10:15.762 --> 01:10:16.595
or anything like that.

01:10:16.595 --> 01:10:18.809
There was nothing to fill up that void.

01:10:18.809 --> 01:10:20.029
- I think the only games
that I've pre-ordered

01:10:20.029 --> 01:10:23.809
are the ones that I know
100% I'm going to love.

01:10:23.809 --> 01:10:26.189
- I've ordered every single
Mario release of late

01:10:26.189 --> 01:10:27.408
and I haven't played any of them.

01:10:27.408 --> 01:10:28.241
(Joey chuckles)

01:10:28.241 --> 01:10:29.427
- Oh, that sounds like
your problem too. (laughs)

01:10:29.427 --> 01:10:31.136
- I don't know why.

01:10:31.136 --> 01:10:32.066
They brainwashed me.

01:10:32.066 --> 01:10:33.522
- I think the last game I pre-ordered

01:10:33.522 --> 01:10:35.892
was "Final Fantasy VII R"

01:10:35.892 --> 01:10:38.064
but I 100-percented that 'cause
I knew I was gonna like it

01:10:38.064 --> 01:10:38.905
'cause I liked the original.

01:10:38.905 --> 01:10:41.097
And "Persona 5 Royal" as
well, I pre-ordered that

01:10:41.097 --> 01:10:43.430
because I liked "Persona 5."

01:10:44.446 --> 01:10:46.194
- I have so many fucking
games that I've bought

01:10:46.194 --> 01:10:47.874
in my library that I just haven't-

01:10:47.874 --> 01:10:49.734
- Oh, yeah, same.
- I've downloaded them,

01:10:49.734 --> 01:10:50.567
I've installed them,

01:10:50.567 --> 01:10:52.464
and I just never opened them.

01:10:52.464 --> 01:10:53.504
Like I've never opened them.

01:10:53.504 --> 01:10:55.772
- When was the last time you
got really hyped for a game?

01:10:55.772 --> 01:10:56.962
- "Final Fantasy VII R" probably.

01:10:56.962 --> 01:10:57.972
- Did it live up to your hype?

01:10:57.972 --> 01:10:58.805
- Yeah, I 100-percented it.

01:10:58.805 --> 01:11:00.471
It was fantastic.
- What about you, Garnt?

01:11:00.471 --> 01:11:01.304
When was the last time
you pre-ordered a game

01:11:01.304 --> 01:11:02.316
and got very excited about it?

01:11:02.316 --> 01:11:03.280
- I haven't pre-ordered...

01:11:03.280 --> 01:11:05.931
Like the last time I got
hyped for a game, "Cyberpunk."

01:11:05.931 --> 01:11:08.431
(Joey and Connor laughing)

01:11:08.431 --> 01:11:09.264
I'm not joking.

01:11:09.264 --> 01:11:11.968
That was the last time
I got hyped for a game.

01:11:11.968 --> 01:11:14.005
- And everybody laughed.
(Connor laughing)

01:11:14.005 --> 01:11:14.838
Everybody laughed.
- That's a good one.

01:11:14.838 --> 01:11:18.118
- And you know why I still
haven't even played it.

01:11:18.118 --> 01:11:19.977
- I beat sci-fi, I don't give a shit.

01:11:19.977 --> 01:11:21.589
It's a fucking terrible game, oh my god.

01:11:21.589 --> 01:11:22.422
(Joey laughs)

01:11:22.422 --> 01:11:24.598
- No, because I was just like,
"Great, it's a sci-fi game,

01:11:24.598 --> 01:11:25.431
it's 'Cyberpunk.'

01:11:25.431 --> 01:11:27.449
this looks like everything
I've ever wanted

01:11:27.449 --> 01:11:28.758
to fill up that void

01:11:28.758 --> 01:11:32.298
that 'Mass Effect' has
just left me for years."

01:11:32.298 --> 01:11:34.018
- And now that hole is
even deeper. (laughs)

01:11:34.018 --> 01:11:35.654
- And now the hole is even fucking deeper.

01:11:35.654 --> 01:11:36.487
- It's a shame

01:11:36.487 --> 01:11:39.820
you couldn't pre-order therapy
with it as well. (laughs)

01:11:39.820 --> 01:11:41.809
- Comes with a free psychiatrist.

01:11:41.809 --> 01:11:43.690
- No, I'm like, every few months,

01:11:43.690 --> 01:11:46.717
I just Google, "Is
Cyberpunk 2077 playable?"

01:11:46.717 --> 01:11:48.017
- I saw a good article.

01:11:48.017 --> 01:11:49.296
It was like,

01:11:49.296 --> 01:11:52.614
"'Cyberpunk' is nowhere near
a 'No Man's Sky' turnaround."

01:11:52.614 --> 01:11:54.575
- (laughs) Oh, brutal.

01:11:54.575 --> 01:11:56.350
- The devs are like, "We're
nowhere near fixing it."

01:11:56.350 --> 01:11:58.983
Like "No Man's Sky" did
something like that,

01:11:58.983 --> 01:12:01.352
according to something like that.

01:12:01.352 --> 01:12:03.431
And they had to say a "No
Man's Sky" turnaround.

01:12:03.431 --> 01:12:04.582
- Well, yeah, of course.
- Oh.

01:12:04.582 --> 01:12:05.415
- I mean that is like,

01:12:05.415 --> 01:12:08.143
"No Man's Sky" is the
fucking anime redemption

01:12:08.143 --> 01:12:09.413
of the gaming industry.

01:12:09.413 --> 01:12:11.450
I think it's one of the only redemption-

01:12:11.450 --> 01:12:13.441
- That's when the antagonists
turned into the protagonists.

01:12:13.441 --> 01:12:14.274
(everyone laughs)

01:12:14.274 --> 01:12:15.663
- Because most companies,
you just cut your losses

01:12:15.663 --> 01:12:18.006
and you're like, "Fuck it, make
the next fucking 'Fallout.'"

01:12:18.006 --> 01:12:18.839
- Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:12:18.839 --> 01:12:21.063
- Fuck 76, make a new one.
You know, that's how it is.

01:12:21.063 --> 01:12:22.392
- Well, when was the
last time you got hyped?

01:12:22.392 --> 01:12:23.225
- Yeah, as the gamer?

01:12:23.225 --> 01:12:24.434
- (sighs) "Borderlands 3."

01:12:24.434 --> 01:12:25.802
I was very hyped for "Borderlands 3."

01:12:25.802 --> 01:12:26.881
- Oh, okay.
- Was it good?

01:12:26.881 --> 01:12:28.261
- Uh, no.
- Oh, really?

01:12:28.261 --> 01:12:29.941
- I was extremely hyped
for "Borderlands 3."

01:12:29.941 --> 01:12:31.805
"Borderlands 2" is one
of my favorite games.

01:12:31.805 --> 01:12:32.638
(Garnt sighs)

01:12:32.638 --> 01:12:33.517
- Yeah, yeah, 'cause I was gonna ask.

01:12:33.517 --> 01:12:34.797
I've never played 3, but I've played 2,

01:12:34.797 --> 01:12:36.135
and 2 was great.
- Have you played 2?

01:12:36.135 --> 01:12:37.056
- I haven't played "Borderlands 2."

01:12:37.056 --> 01:12:38.288
- What was the sigh there, Garnt?

01:12:38.288 --> 01:12:39.467
That was a dramatic sigh.

01:12:39.467 --> 01:12:41.262
- I just realized what the game

01:12:41.262 --> 01:12:43.494
before "Cyberpunk 2077-"
- Okay, we'll get into it.

01:12:43.494 --> 01:12:45.233
- What the last game I
was hyped before that.

01:12:45.233 --> 01:12:46.312
- "Borderlands 2," right?

01:12:46.312 --> 01:12:47.932
I loved "Borderlands."

01:12:47.932 --> 01:12:50.442
So I bought "Borderlands
1" originally on Xbox 360,

01:12:50.442 --> 01:12:52.281
and I thought it was shit.

01:12:52.281 --> 01:12:54.371
I hated it 'cause I didn't
have friends to play with.

01:12:54.371 --> 01:12:55.634
So it was a terrible game to play alone.

01:12:55.634 --> 01:12:57.871
But when I finally went
back to it, months later,

01:12:57.871 --> 01:13:02.673
my friends bought 'cause it
went on more sale, cheap as art,

01:13:02.673 --> 01:13:03.971
and, yeah, I loved it.

01:13:03.971 --> 01:13:06.052
I thought, "Wow, okay,
this game is actually sick

01:13:06.052 --> 01:13:06.952
when you play it with friends."

01:13:06.952 --> 01:13:07.908
Then "Borderlands 2" came out

01:13:07.908 --> 01:13:09.152
and it looked like they
just improved everything.

01:13:09.152 --> 01:13:10.175
And they did.

01:13:10.175 --> 01:13:11.231
And it was amazing.

01:13:11.231 --> 01:13:13.041
"Borderlands 2" is such a good game

01:13:13.041 --> 01:13:15.006
and playing it with friends is amazing.

01:13:15.006 --> 01:13:18.420
Like this game is so much
replay value with friends.

01:13:18.420 --> 01:13:20.780
And I absolutely had some
of the best gaming memories

01:13:20.780 --> 01:13:21.613
playing "Borderlands 2."

01:13:21.613 --> 01:13:22.558
So naturally,

01:13:22.558 --> 01:13:23.720
"Borderlands 3" was coming out

01:13:23.720 --> 01:13:26.323
and I had a monster
gaming PC, I was ready.

01:13:26.323 --> 01:13:28.228
All my friends were getting it.

01:13:28.228 --> 01:13:29.518
There was endless people
I could play with.

01:13:29.518 --> 01:13:30.955
It was gonna be good.

01:13:30.955 --> 01:13:32.258
So I play it and, yeah,

01:13:32.258 --> 01:13:33.928
it's just kind of like "Borderlands 2"

01:13:33.928 --> 01:13:35.568
but with a worse story.

01:13:35.568 --> 01:13:37.665
Like the stuff they add isn't very good.

01:13:37.665 --> 01:13:39.913
- Wait, since when have you
fucking cared about story?

01:13:39.913 --> 01:13:41.942
- Well, "Borderlands 2"
actually was such like...

01:13:41.942 --> 01:13:44.903
Handsome Jack is such an engaging villain.

01:13:44.903 --> 01:13:46.703
But even when you don't
care about the story,

01:13:46.703 --> 01:13:48.133
he's there, always making you laugh.

01:13:48.133 --> 01:13:49.799
- [Joey] Right.
- And that was something that,

01:13:49.799 --> 01:13:50.632
even if I didn't care what was happening,

01:13:50.632 --> 01:13:51.924
I knew that I liked Handsome Jack

01:13:51.924 --> 01:13:53.103
and that he was funny as fuck.

01:13:53.103 --> 01:13:54.301
But I loved having that.

01:13:54.301 --> 01:13:55.291
And the two main villains

01:13:55.291 --> 01:13:58.690
were YouTubers or Twitch
streamers in the third one.

01:13:58.690 --> 01:13:59.523
- Right.
- It was just cringe

01:13:59.523 --> 01:14:00.821
'cause I'm a YouTuber and Twitch streamer,

01:14:00.821 --> 01:14:02.228
so it was cringe watching them like-

01:14:02.228 --> 01:14:05.382
- I am the bad guy. (laughs)
(Joey laughs)

01:14:05.382 --> 01:14:07.843
- It was just like poking
fun at me in the worst way.

01:14:07.843 --> 01:14:08.676
- [Joey] Right, right.

01:14:08.676 --> 01:14:09.572
- And I was like, "This isn't this funny."

01:14:09.572 --> 01:14:11.311
- This isn't the
representation I asked for.

01:14:11.311 --> 01:14:13.624
- (laughs) This is slander.
(Garnt laughs)

01:14:13.624 --> 01:14:14.457
- I'm all down

01:14:14.457 --> 01:14:16.667
for when people make fun of
YouTubers and Twitch streamers.

01:14:16.667 --> 01:14:17.576
I'm all down for it.

01:14:17.576 --> 01:14:19.795
But sometimes they do it in a way where-

01:14:19.795 --> 01:14:20.628
- Distasteful way, yeah.

01:14:20.628 --> 01:14:22.548
- In a way where you've
clearly never watched something

01:14:22.548 --> 01:14:23.434
because there are so many other things

01:14:23.434 --> 01:14:25.084
you could have gone for.

01:14:25.084 --> 01:14:26.209
You know, they do the whole thing

01:14:26.209 --> 01:14:28.109
of like, "Oh, hi, guys," whatever,

01:14:28.109 --> 01:14:29.009
and they could have gone for like,

01:14:29.009 --> 01:14:30.758
"Why don't you thank me
for the $10 donation?"

01:14:30.758 --> 01:14:31.683
or something like that.

01:14:31.683 --> 01:14:32.653
That would've been funny as fuck.

01:14:32.653 --> 01:14:34.503
You know, like Bo Burnham
did a great parody of it.

01:14:34.503 --> 01:14:37.105
I mean, Bo Burnham used to
be a YouTuber, so obviously.

01:14:37.105 --> 01:14:38.932
He did a great parody of
Twitch streamers and stuff,

01:14:38.932 --> 01:14:39.765
and that was great,

01:14:39.765 --> 01:14:42.085
but I felt like it was a terrible parody

01:14:42.085 --> 01:14:44.324
and it was also, they
were just so unlikable

01:14:44.324 --> 01:14:46.339
and there's so many bugs in it as well.

01:14:46.339 --> 01:14:48.117
Like there's so many game-breaking bugs

01:14:48.117 --> 01:14:49.125
that just happened throughout.

01:14:49.125 --> 01:14:51.285
And I was like, "This
shouldn't be happening.

01:14:51.285 --> 01:14:52.584
I waited years for this.

01:14:52.584 --> 01:14:53.946
I got hyped for this.

01:14:53.946 --> 01:14:55.086
I felt invested in this."

01:14:55.086 --> 01:14:56.316
- Give my hype back.

01:14:56.316 --> 01:14:57.476
- Also I didn't really
like any of the characters

01:14:57.476 --> 01:14:58.316
that you could play as.

01:14:58.316 --> 01:14:59.982
- Yeah.
- Which kind of sucked.

01:14:59.982 --> 01:15:00.835
"Borderlands 2," I felt
like every single character

01:15:00.835 --> 01:15:03.414
was like Pog.
- Yeah.

01:15:03.414 --> 01:15:05.426
- That's how I got burnt.

01:15:05.426 --> 01:15:08.939
- The game I got hyped for
before "Cyberpunk" was...

01:15:08.939 --> 01:15:10.199
This just shows my track record

01:15:10.199 --> 01:15:11.899
and why I don't get
hyped for games anymore.

01:15:11.899 --> 01:15:13.398
It was "Mass Effect: Andromeda."

01:15:13.398 --> 01:15:14.667
- I thought you were
about to say "Fallout 76."

01:15:14.667 --> 01:15:16.274
(Garnt and Joey laughs)

01:15:16.274 --> 01:15:18.254
- I thought you were
gonna say "No Man's Sky."

01:15:18.254 --> 01:15:20.874
- Garnt's like, "'No
Man's Sky,' 'Fallout 76,'

01:15:20.874 --> 01:15:23.040
'Mass Effect: Andromeda.'"
(Garnt laughs)

01:15:23.040 --> 01:15:23.942
I love Dunkey's video.

01:15:23.942 --> 01:15:25.635
I've never played "Mass Effect."

01:15:25.635 --> 01:15:27.090
I've just watched Dunkey's videos on them.

01:15:27.090 --> 01:15:28.928
And his video on "Andromeda" is so funny.

01:15:28.928 --> 01:15:30.018
- I think I've played like an hour

01:15:30.018 --> 01:15:31.077
of "Mass Effect: Andromeda"

01:15:31.077 --> 01:15:33.632
and I'm just like, "This
just isn't doing it for me."

01:15:33.632 --> 01:15:35.020
- [Joey] Right.

01:15:35.020 --> 01:15:36.641
- By that point,

01:15:36.641 --> 01:15:39.153
I think "Cyberpunk" was just a, yeah,

01:15:39.153 --> 01:15:42.477
this looks like a game
that could appeal to me,

01:15:42.477 --> 01:15:43.417
but I think "Mass Effect"

01:15:43.417 --> 01:15:45.374
was really what just killed my soul

01:15:45.374 --> 01:15:46.334
inside of me. (chuckles)
- Right, right.

01:15:46.334 --> 01:15:49.148
- There's something so
heartbreaking about it

01:15:49.148 --> 01:15:51.093
in a way that I've never experienced,

01:15:51.093 --> 01:15:52.928
where the game just
lets you down like that.

01:15:52.928 --> 01:15:53.761
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

01:15:53.761 --> 01:15:55.988
- It feels like your dad just
never came home, you know?

01:15:55.988 --> 01:15:57.241
Like it's like, damn.

01:15:57.241 --> 01:15:58.481
- But it's like, it feels
like your dad came home,

01:15:58.481 --> 01:16:01.518
but with a different woman.
(everyone laughs)

01:16:01.518 --> 01:16:04.307
- A new son.
(everyone laughs)

01:16:04.307 --> 01:16:06.390
This is you now, alright?

01:16:07.971 --> 01:16:09.202
I feel like that's the first time

01:16:09.202 --> 01:16:12.990
you get to really experience
betrayal as a young adult.

01:16:12.990 --> 01:16:14.130
A true betrayal.
(Garnt giggling)

01:16:14.130 --> 01:16:16.500
- I trusted you. I followed
you all the way through,

01:16:16.500 --> 01:16:17.759
and this is how you repay me?

01:16:17.759 --> 01:16:18.822
- I stuck with you for years.

01:16:18.822 --> 01:16:20.957
I had memories with you that I can't,

01:16:20.957 --> 01:16:22.697
I've never even had with anyone else,

01:16:22.697 --> 01:16:24.545
and this is how you repay me?

01:16:24.545 --> 01:16:26.383
It's gone like that.
- Yeah.

01:16:26.383 --> 01:16:28.162
- Yeah, I mean,

01:16:28.162 --> 01:16:30.242
now I just try to keep as little knowledge

01:16:30.242 --> 01:16:32.902
of the gaming industry and
what's coming out as possible

01:16:32.902 --> 01:16:34.720
because I've kind of realized

01:16:34.720 --> 01:16:36.520
my favorite gaming experiences recently

01:16:36.520 --> 01:16:38.942
have just been games
that I had no idea about

01:16:38.942 --> 01:16:40.062
until they were out.

01:16:40.062 --> 01:16:41.380
- I didn't know anything
about "Breath of the Wild"

01:16:41.380 --> 01:16:42.706
and it blew me away.
- Yeah, exactly.

01:16:42.706 --> 01:16:43.735
- Yeah, didn't know anything
about "Breath of the Wild."

01:16:43.735 --> 01:16:45.335
I'm just like, it's been fucking,

01:16:45.335 --> 01:16:47.337
I hadn't played Zelda since "Wind Waker"

01:16:47.337 --> 01:16:48.965
and it was fucking amazing.
- Oh yeah.

01:16:48.965 --> 01:16:50.092
"Horizon Zero Dawn"?

01:16:50.092 --> 01:16:51.172
I was like, "What the fuck?

01:16:51.172 --> 01:16:52.842
What kind of game franchise is this?"

01:16:52.842 --> 01:16:54.342
I had no idea what it was about.

01:16:54.342 --> 01:16:55.417
It was fucking amazing.

01:16:55.417 --> 01:16:56.326
- That's why I'm not hyping myself up

01:16:56.326 --> 01:16:57.447
for "Breath of the Wild 2," right?

01:16:57.447 --> 01:17:00.742
Because I don't want a
fucking "Andromeda" to happen.

01:17:00.742 --> 01:17:01.575
(Garnt laughs)

01:17:01.575 --> 01:17:02.408
- Like God forbid it ever happens,

01:17:02.408 --> 01:17:03.272
but you never know, right?

01:17:03.272 --> 01:17:04.665
So I'm just gonna wait.

01:17:04.665 --> 01:17:05.725
I'm just gonna wait.

01:17:05.725 --> 01:17:07.244
- Yeah, and also like,

01:17:07.244 --> 01:17:09.604
obviously everyone's streaming a lot now.

01:17:09.604 --> 01:17:11.637
You know, when E3 happens or
a Nintendo press conference,

01:17:11.637 --> 01:17:12.693
everyone's like, "Oh, did you watch it?

01:17:12.693 --> 01:17:14.247
Did you watch the E3 conference?"

01:17:14.247 --> 01:17:16.340
Why would I watch an hour of ads?

01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:17.173
Why?
(Joey laughs)

01:17:17.173 --> 01:17:18.150
What, so I can get excited

01:17:18.150 --> 01:17:20.139
and give my money to a company
that's gonna let me down?

01:17:20.139 --> 01:17:21.550
No. No, thank you.

01:17:21.550 --> 01:17:23.645
When the game comes out and I
hear it's good, I'll buy it.

01:17:23.645 --> 01:17:26.235
- Yeah, why would I sit down
and watch an hour conference

01:17:26.235 --> 01:17:27.505
of getting myself hyped for something

01:17:27.505 --> 01:17:29.335
that I probably won't be hyped about?

01:17:29.335 --> 01:17:30.635
- I don't know, I think it's pretty fun.

01:17:30.635 --> 01:17:32.428
I'm not even invested in it.
- Sometimes it's fun.

01:17:32.428 --> 01:17:33.872
- I'm just like, sometimes when...

01:17:33.872 --> 01:17:35.845
Like I still remember

01:17:35.845 --> 01:17:37.983
when "Final Fantasy VII
Remake" was announced

01:17:37.983 --> 01:17:39.413
and just the reaction around that.

01:17:39.413 --> 01:17:42.702
I'm just like, I don't give
a shit about "Final Fantasy,"

01:17:42.702 --> 01:17:44.750
but I'm fucking hyped.

01:17:44.750 --> 01:17:46.259
- Never mind me who never
played "Final Fantasy."

01:17:46.259 --> 01:17:47.261
I'm like, "What's going on?

01:17:47.261 --> 01:17:48.186
What's going on?"
(Garnt laughs)

01:17:48.186 --> 01:17:51.945
- Meanwhile, I was the one
going, "Yeah," in the crowd.

01:17:51.945 --> 01:17:52.778
- Yeah, and then they get announced

01:17:52.778 --> 01:17:55.209
"Shenmue III" afterwards.
(Joey laughs)

01:17:55.209 --> 01:17:56.069
(laughs) I was just like,

01:17:56.069 --> 01:17:57.869
"What kind of a press conference is this?"

01:17:57.869 --> 01:17:59.603
Like, I think I was more
hyped about press conference

01:17:59.603 --> 01:18:01.183
than the actual games themselves.

01:18:01.183 --> 01:18:02.016
- Yeah, "Shenmue III,"

01:18:02.016 --> 01:18:04.330
that turned out to be a great game, huh.

01:18:04.330 --> 01:18:08.507
- But I feel like it's a fun little event,

01:18:08.507 --> 01:18:10.087
you know, if you take part of it.

01:18:10.087 --> 01:18:11.488
I just feel like-

01:18:11.488 --> 01:18:12.503
- I just don't wanna get hyped.

01:18:12.503 --> 01:18:13.726
- It's like the Nintendo Directs, right?

01:18:13.726 --> 01:18:14.561
That's like another one

01:18:14.561 --> 01:18:15.589
where it's just like, "Did you watch it?

01:18:15.589 --> 01:18:17.028
Did you watch the Nintendo Direct?"

01:18:17.028 --> 01:18:18.027
- There's something about Nintendo Directs

01:18:18.027 --> 01:18:19.337
that really pissed me off.

01:18:19.337 --> 01:18:20.387
I can't put my finger on it.

01:18:20.387 --> 01:18:21.841
I get angry watching Nintendo Direct.

01:18:21.841 --> 01:18:22.768
- (chuckles) Why?
- I don't know why.

01:18:22.768 --> 01:18:23.968
I think it's the way they present games

01:18:23.968 --> 01:18:26.197
that clearly no one gives a shit about.

01:18:26.197 --> 01:18:29.540
They'll be like, "And
now is 'Just Dance 17.'"

01:18:29.540 --> 01:18:31.620
(Joey laughs)
And it's like, why?

01:18:31.620 --> 01:18:33.008
- But they always have to sandwich it

01:18:33.008 --> 01:18:34.691
between two big titles, right?
- Yeah.

01:18:34.691 --> 01:18:35.991
- Which is fair enough, right?
- I understand.

01:18:35.991 --> 01:18:37.051
- They clearly know,

01:18:37.051 --> 01:18:39.988
but it's also just like, I don't
care about "Just Dance 76."

01:18:39.988 --> 01:18:42.024
- Well, sometimes they
do ad spots, I think,

01:18:42.024 --> 01:18:43.332
for other companies to,

01:18:43.332 --> 01:18:45.352
where they give, I think it's an ad spot.

01:18:45.352 --> 01:18:46.564
I think they do this.

01:18:46.564 --> 01:18:48.823
And that they'll show
a game that looks awful

01:18:48.823 --> 01:18:51.408
for like 30 minutes and
they'll do a play-through.

01:18:51.408 --> 01:18:53.916
And I'm like, "Stop this,
stop this right now.

01:18:53.916 --> 01:18:55.655
Show me an ad. Show me
an ad over this, please.

01:18:55.655 --> 01:18:57.677
(Joey laughs)
Anything else other than this.

01:18:57.677 --> 01:18:58.672
I can't stand this.

01:18:58.672 --> 01:19:00.364
- Show me a Bud Light ad.

01:19:00.364 --> 01:19:02.205
- I'll take it.
- I'll take a Bud Light ad.

01:19:02.205 --> 01:19:04.275
- Give me a "Fallout
76" demo or something.

01:19:04.275 --> 01:19:05.574
God damn it, please, I'm
begging for something else.

01:19:05.574 --> 01:19:06.826
I don't know.

01:19:06.826 --> 01:19:07.913
I don't know.

01:19:07.913 --> 01:19:09.244
I think I'm just getting
to that point in my life

01:19:09.244 --> 01:19:10.510
where I'm becoming extremely
bitter about everything

01:19:10.510 --> 01:19:13.063
that makes other people happy.

01:19:13.063 --> 01:19:15.023
- (laughs) Welcome to adulting.

01:19:15.023 --> 01:19:16.143
- I think I'm getting to that point.

01:19:16.143 --> 01:19:17.273
- It's called being adulting

01:19:17.273 --> 01:19:19.164
and it's called being British as well.

01:19:19.164 --> 01:19:20.414
It's like the worst combination.

01:19:20.414 --> 01:19:21.953
- An old angry bastard is all you become.

01:19:21.953 --> 01:19:24.353
- I think I sit there on my
porch, just rocking my chair,

01:19:24.353 --> 01:19:26.683
thinking, "Oh, you young kids
getting excited over games,

01:19:26.683 --> 01:19:28.483
how naive of you."

01:19:28.483 --> 01:19:30.263
- Imagine being happy.

01:19:30.263 --> 01:19:31.498
Imagine being excited.
- How naive of you.

01:19:31.498 --> 01:19:33.718
- If only I could feel
these emotions anymore.

01:19:33.718 --> 01:19:35.645
- Oh, you think "Mario
Golf" is gonna be fun?

01:19:35.645 --> 01:19:36.478
Really?

01:19:36.478 --> 01:19:37.543
Have fun playing "Mario Golf."

01:19:37.543 --> 01:19:39.787
One time at a party and they're
never playing it ever again.

01:19:39.787 --> 01:19:40.630
(Garnt laughs)

01:19:40.630 --> 01:19:42.602
"Mario Tennis," you thought that was fun?

01:19:42.602 --> 01:19:44.947
I never felt angrier than
when I bought "Mario Tennis,"

01:19:44.947 --> 01:19:46.042
the new "Mario Tennis."
- Right.

01:19:46.042 --> 01:19:46.967
- It's a fucking terrible game.

01:19:46.967 --> 01:19:47.800
Have you played it?

01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:48.633
- Yeah, I like it.

01:19:48.633 --> 01:19:49.466
- It's terrible, it's terrible.

01:19:49.466 --> 01:19:50.299
- Why?
- Well, why is it terrible?

01:19:50.299 --> 01:19:51.517
- Wait, have you played
the original though?

01:19:51.517 --> 01:19:52.350
- No.

01:19:52.350 --> 01:19:53.447
- Well, that's probably why. (laughs)

01:19:53.447 --> 01:19:54.341
- Why?

01:19:54.341 --> 01:19:55.854
I have to have prerequisite
knowledge of another game?

01:19:55.854 --> 01:19:58.137
- Well, compared to the
original, it's much better.

01:19:58.137 --> 01:19:59.803
- I loved the original.
- I like the original too,

01:19:59.803 --> 01:20:01.534
but I think the new one
just improved on it.

01:20:01.534 --> 01:20:03.315
- I mean, I loved the
original 'cause I was a kid

01:20:03.315 --> 01:20:05.854
and I had zero taste in video games.

01:20:05.854 --> 01:20:06.694
Everything was fine.
(Joey laughs)

01:20:06.694 --> 01:20:07.848
- I'm sure I pissed off a lot.

01:20:07.848 --> 01:20:09.657
- I'm sorry I don't have
taste in video games, wow.

01:20:09.657 --> 01:20:11.414
- I'm sure I pissed people
off saying it's terrible.

01:20:11.414 --> 01:20:12.247
I played it

01:20:12.247 --> 01:20:15.695
and I was so bored out of
my mind playing this game.

01:20:15.695 --> 01:20:16.528
- Well, I mean,

01:20:16.528 --> 01:20:17.463
clearly it's just not a
game made for you, right?

01:20:17.463 --> 01:20:18.364
- Why?

01:20:18.364 --> 01:20:19.197
Why is it not?

01:20:19.197 --> 01:20:20.030
I would have loved this.

01:20:20.030 --> 01:20:20.863
What's going on?

01:20:20.863 --> 01:20:22.529
What's going on? Why do I hate this game?

01:20:22.529 --> 01:20:24.015
- You sound like the same crowd of people-

01:20:24.015 --> 01:20:24.974
- 'Cause it's not toxic enough for you.

01:20:24.974 --> 01:20:26.974
- You sound like the same crowd
of people who are pissed off

01:20:26.974 --> 01:20:29.426
when Nintendo released the Nintendo 2DS,

01:20:29.426 --> 01:20:31.286
which was intended for
like, five-year-olds.

01:20:31.286 --> 01:20:32.570
(Garnt and Connor laughs)

01:20:32.570 --> 01:20:35.481
How dare Nintendo not release
a console made for me?

01:20:35.481 --> 01:20:36.314
- I like the 2DS.

01:20:36.314 --> 01:20:38.017
I thought it was affordable and, yeah,

01:20:38.017 --> 01:20:39.274
I liked the ergonomics of it.

01:20:39.274 --> 01:20:40.107
It looked cool.

01:20:40.107 --> 01:20:42.174
- It looked like a fucking Fisher Price,

01:20:42.174 --> 01:20:43.425
fucking like children's toy.
- Yeah, I liked it.

01:20:43.425 --> 01:20:46.415
- And adults are like,
"What the fuck, Nintendo?

01:20:46.415 --> 01:20:47.445
How dare you not make?

01:20:47.445 --> 01:20:48.278
What is this?

01:20:48.278 --> 01:20:50.396
I'm not gonna buy this."
- How dare you make a toy?

01:20:50.396 --> 01:20:52.123
What are you, a toy company?

01:20:52.123 --> 01:20:53.356
- I'm not one of those people
who gets angry at Nintendo

01:20:53.356 --> 01:20:55.916
for not making adult-oriented products,

01:20:55.916 --> 01:20:57.216
'cause that's not what they do.

01:20:57.216 --> 01:20:58.929
But, you know, for stuff like Pokemon,

01:20:58.929 --> 01:21:01.426
I wish that they would
put a difficulty option

01:21:01.426 --> 01:21:05.116
or something where you could
add something, like that.

01:21:05.116 --> 01:21:06.375
I wish they would include something.

01:21:06.375 --> 01:21:09.409
- The toxic gamer is coming out right now.

01:21:09.409 --> 01:21:11.224
- Is it insane of me to ask Pokemon

01:21:11.224 --> 01:21:14.170
to include something that
makes it more difficult?

01:21:14.170 --> 01:21:15.470
- Are you talking about "Pokemon Unite"?

01:21:15.470 --> 01:21:16.503
- No, no, no, no.

01:21:16.503 --> 01:21:17.788
- Or just Pokemon in general?
- The normal Pokemon.

01:21:17.788 --> 01:21:19.004
- Well, the great thing about Pokemon

01:21:19.004 --> 01:21:21.495
is that you can make it as
difficult as you fucking want.

01:21:21.495 --> 01:21:22.775
That's the beauty of the game.
- Yeah, that's true.

01:21:22.775 --> 01:21:24.075
- That's why Nuzlockes are a thing.

01:21:24.075 --> 01:21:24.908
- I know, I know,

01:21:24.908 --> 01:21:27.509
but I wish there was a way
the in-game was baked into it

01:21:27.509 --> 01:21:28.756
that allows you to make it more difficult

01:21:28.756 --> 01:21:29.825
or to do certain things.

01:21:29.825 --> 01:21:30.917
I don't understand why-

01:21:30.917 --> 01:21:32.984
- No, I don't think that's-
- I disagree with that.

01:21:32.984 --> 01:21:33.817
- I disagree,

01:21:33.817 --> 01:21:37.415
because I think purposely
leaving it open-ended

01:21:37.415 --> 01:21:38.694
to how difficult you want it

01:21:38.694 --> 01:21:41.074
is what makes that game
so appealing to people.

01:21:41.074 --> 01:21:42.135
If you put a difficulty...

01:21:42.135 --> 01:21:44.284
Like if you went into a Pokemon game

01:21:44.284 --> 01:21:46.054
and you were like,
"Choose the difficulty,"

01:21:46.054 --> 01:21:48.084
immediately people will be like, "Oh."

01:21:48.084 --> 01:21:51.118
- Okay, actually, in
regards to difficulty,

01:21:51.118 --> 01:21:52.808
I fucking hate choosing difficulty.

01:21:52.808 --> 01:21:54.739
I hate it so much.
- I do hate it too.

01:21:54.739 --> 01:21:55.572
- I hate it as well.
- It depends on the game.

01:21:55.572 --> 01:21:56.528
It depends on the game,

01:21:56.528 --> 01:21:58.041
because on some games,

01:21:58.041 --> 01:22:00.118
it's completely stupid
and unnecessary, right?

01:22:00.118 --> 01:22:01.358
Like first person shooters,

01:22:01.358 --> 01:22:03.658
I hate it because it just
makes them more bullock-spongy.

01:22:03.658 --> 01:22:04.491
- Yeah.

01:22:04.491 --> 01:22:06.162
- That's all it does. But
on some games like Pokemon

01:22:06.162 --> 01:22:07.908
where it's like, okay,

01:22:07.908 --> 01:22:10.670
even a 12-year-old would
probably find this too easy,

01:22:10.670 --> 01:22:11.589
like especially the new one.

01:22:11.589 --> 01:22:12.705
The new one was like mind-

01:22:12.705 --> 01:22:14.320
- Well, the new one's hold
your hand, that's why.

01:22:14.320 --> 01:22:16.004
- It was beyond mind...

01:22:16.004 --> 01:22:18.160
Like even like, you know,
you play "Platinum"-

01:22:18.160 --> 01:22:20.203
- That's a problem with
the game itself, right?

01:22:20.203 --> 01:22:21.143
It's just not difficult enough.

01:22:21.143 --> 01:22:24.677
- Yeah, I feel like even adding
10% more difficulty to this

01:22:24.677 --> 01:22:25.576
is like, what?

01:22:25.576 --> 01:22:26.409
Like with "Pokemon Platinum,"

01:22:26.409 --> 01:22:28.196
I was playing that, I did a Nuzlocke,

01:22:28.196 --> 01:22:29.476
but even the core game itself

01:22:29.476 --> 01:22:31.796
was actually kind of challenging.

01:22:31.796 --> 01:22:34.461
You can't just fall asleep
and just spam one Pokemon.

01:22:34.461 --> 01:22:35.294
- Well, that's the thing, right?

01:22:35.294 --> 01:22:37.130
It's like, I feel that's the
problem with just Pokemon games

01:22:37.130 --> 01:22:37.963
in general where like...

01:22:37.963 --> 01:22:39.504
Like I played "Sun and Moon."

01:22:39.504 --> 01:22:42.108
That shit holds your hand the entire way,

01:22:42.108 --> 01:22:43.007
even as an adult.
- It's so insulting.

01:22:43.007 --> 01:22:44.270
- And I'm like, dude,

01:22:44.270 --> 01:22:46.057
like ten-year-old me was crying,

01:22:46.057 --> 01:22:49.211
trying to get past the
June 3 of silver, right?

01:22:49.211 --> 01:22:50.341
And the game didn't give a fuck.

01:22:50.341 --> 01:22:51.911
It was just like, "Just get good."

01:22:51.911 --> 01:22:53.704
- It's like, "Figure it out, you're 10.

01:22:53.704 --> 01:22:55.630
You should start thinking, bro.

01:22:55.630 --> 01:22:57.801
Use that fucking 10-year-old
thick skull of yours."

01:22:57.801 --> 01:23:00.047
- Yeah, exactly.
- I feel like nowadays,

01:23:00.047 --> 01:23:01.205
people have less patience

01:23:01.205 --> 01:23:02.482
when it comes to completing games, man.

01:23:02.482 --> 01:23:04.566
There's no way-
- But, oh, come on.

01:23:04.566 --> 01:23:07.443
Making a Pokemon gym slightly harder

01:23:07.443 --> 01:23:09.364
is hardly asking for like...

01:23:09.364 --> 01:23:11.364
We're not adding in "Dark
Souls" level of difficulty

01:23:11.364 --> 01:23:13.114
to a children's game.

01:23:14.913 --> 01:23:16.212
You should in a Pokemon game,

01:23:16.212 --> 01:23:17.593
I think even if you're like 10 years old,

01:23:17.593 --> 01:23:20.056
you should fail the first gym probably

01:23:20.056 --> 01:23:22.596
and be forced to be like, "Maybe
I should buy some potions.

01:23:22.596 --> 01:23:24.496
Maybe I should consider doing something.

01:23:24.496 --> 01:23:25.775
Not just fucking steamrolling this shit

01:23:25.775 --> 01:23:27.216
with my Mudkip every time."

01:23:27.216 --> 01:23:28.850
- Yeah, just give it good game design

01:23:28.850 --> 01:23:30.733
so that you don't have to say anything

01:23:30.733 --> 01:23:34.751
to get the player to figure it out, right?

01:23:34.751 --> 01:23:37.695
- Even when I was a much younger kid,

01:23:37.695 --> 01:23:39.867
you know, when I was 10,
whatever, playing these games,

01:23:39.867 --> 01:23:43.108
I hated it when games were
completely steamrolling,

01:23:43.108 --> 01:23:44.867
like you could just do
it without thinking.

01:23:44.867 --> 01:23:47.698
It's like, having some form
of difficulty there is good.

01:23:47.698 --> 01:23:50.082
And it's also important, I
think, for the kid to learn

01:23:50.082 --> 01:23:51.725
that not everything is
gonna be fucking easy.

01:23:51.725 --> 01:23:52.558
- Yeah, exactly.

01:23:52.558 --> 01:23:54.985
Like I remember when I was
fucking eight years old

01:23:54.985 --> 01:23:56.824
playing "Mega Man 2" for the first time.

01:23:56.824 --> 01:23:59.420
And I was like, "This
is fucking impossible.

01:23:59.420 --> 01:24:00.394
No one can beat this game."

01:24:00.394 --> 01:24:01.388
- Dude, I fucking love that game though.

01:24:01.388 --> 01:24:02.845
- It's one of my favorite
games of all time

01:24:02.845 --> 01:24:06.791
because I learned success through failure.

01:24:06.791 --> 01:24:08.981
- Kids have it too easy nowadays, guys.

01:24:08.981 --> 01:24:09.814
- The problem is, right,

01:24:09.814 --> 01:24:10.647
is that, as an adult,

01:24:10.647 --> 01:24:11.778
I have absolutely zero patience

01:24:11.778 --> 01:24:13.058
for games that are bullshit hard.

01:24:13.058 --> 01:24:13.891
- Right.
- Yeah.

01:24:13.891 --> 01:24:14.724
- Kids do not.

01:24:14.724 --> 01:24:16.497
Kids will play the bullshit hard game

01:24:16.497 --> 01:24:17.737
over and over and over again

01:24:17.737 --> 01:24:18.577
because it's, one,

01:24:18.577 --> 01:24:19.857
it's probably the only
game they're getting,

01:24:19.857 --> 01:24:21.461
and also they love it.
- But it's not anymore.

01:24:21.461 --> 01:24:22.980
It's not.

01:24:22.980 --> 01:24:24.049
- That's the problem, it's not anymore.

01:24:24.049 --> 01:24:25.237
- That's the point I'm trying to make.

01:24:25.237 --> 01:24:26.453
- Well, I mean, if you're
mobile gaming, right?

01:24:26.453 --> 01:24:27.286
- [Joey] Yeah.

01:24:27.286 --> 01:24:28.442
- No, because I feel like there's just,

01:24:28.442 --> 01:24:29.743
games are a lot more affordable nowadays.

01:24:29.743 --> 01:24:33.881
Back then, you had one game
every few months maybe.

01:24:33.881 --> 01:24:34.895
- But there's still,

01:24:34.895 --> 01:24:36.165
if they're getting like
an Xbox or something,

01:24:36.165 --> 01:24:37.970
okay, yeah, they can play
"Fortnite" for free on it.

01:24:37.970 --> 01:24:40.313
But if they wanna buy another
game and it's difficult,

01:24:40.313 --> 01:24:42.100
they're probably gonna try and complete it

01:24:42.100 --> 01:24:44.140
'cause they bought the game or
they wanted it for Christmas

01:24:44.140 --> 01:24:44.973
or something.
- Right.

01:24:44.973 --> 01:24:47.160
Adults try to understand kids. (laughs)

01:24:47.160 --> 01:24:49.580
- No, I'm just thinking
from my perspective.

01:24:49.580 --> 01:24:51.466
I don't know. I mean, most
of them are just happy

01:24:51.466 --> 01:24:52.736
with "Fortnite" and stuff, right?

01:24:52.736 --> 01:24:53.596
- Right, right.
- Yeah.

01:24:53.596 --> 01:24:54.856
- But I mean, you know.

01:24:54.856 --> 01:24:55.856
- I think the other thing as well

01:24:55.856 --> 01:24:58.289
is that at least with the
old games is that, you know,

01:24:58.289 --> 01:25:01.073
because they could only be so long,

01:25:01.073 --> 01:25:02.316
that they literally had
to be like, alright,

01:25:02.316 --> 01:25:04.483
this game, if you blast through it,

01:25:04.483 --> 01:25:05.723
you can probably complete
it in less than an hour.

01:25:05.723 --> 01:25:06.653
- Exactly.

01:25:06.653 --> 01:25:08.693
- But like, we want you to
play this game for a long time

01:25:08.693 --> 01:25:10.423
so we're just gonna make it bullshit hard

01:25:10.423 --> 01:25:12.443
to the point where 40 minutes of gameplay

01:25:12.443 --> 01:25:13.763
is gonna take you about 40 days.

01:25:13.763 --> 01:25:15.993
- Oh, there are a lot of bullshit moments

01:25:15.993 --> 01:25:17.247
in a lot of older games.
- Oh, yeah.

01:25:17.247 --> 01:25:18.972
- And I remember thinking back

01:25:18.972 --> 01:25:22.353
and I'm thinking, "How the fuck did I play

01:25:22.353 --> 01:25:25.119
so many levels of 'Battletoad'

01:25:25.119 --> 01:25:26.244
and 'Contra'-
(Joey laughs)

01:25:26.244 --> 01:25:27.106
- Did you actually play "Battletoad"?

01:25:27.106 --> 01:25:28.423
- I did play "Battletoad."
- Oh my god.

01:25:28.423 --> 01:25:30.011
- It's actually a really
fucking good game.

01:25:30.011 --> 01:25:30.844
- Oh, it's a good game.

01:25:30.844 --> 01:25:31.731
- Yeah, it's fucking great game.

01:25:31.731 --> 01:25:33.551
- It's the shit.

01:25:33.551 --> 01:25:35.351
- Like to this day,

01:25:35.351 --> 01:25:38.885
I remember playing the
fucking motorbike, like the-

01:25:38.885 --> 01:25:40.749
