getting a fucking cramp here

01:26:09.577 --> 01:26:11.896
from just doing the wall jump."

01:26:11.896 --> 01:26:13.171
Jesus Christ.

01:26:13.171 --> 01:26:14.851
My God. (laughs)

01:26:14.851 --> 01:26:15.815
- It's great though, I love it.

01:26:15.815 --> 01:26:17.961
- I guess I'm angry that I'm getting older

01:26:17.961 --> 01:26:19.862
and these children games
aren't getting older with me.

01:26:19.862 --> 01:26:21.006
- Yeah.
- I guess so.

01:26:21.006 --> 01:26:23.589
- I mean, like with difficulty,

01:26:24.476 --> 01:26:27.945
I now like when a game has
just one set difficulty,

01:26:27.945 --> 01:26:28.846
even if it's easy,

01:26:28.846 --> 01:26:33.734
even if it's steamrolling.
- No, I agree, I agree.

01:26:33.734 --> 01:26:35.414
- I get anxious that

01:26:35.414 --> 01:26:36.865
with any game or any piece of media

01:26:36.865 --> 01:26:39.606
where I want to enjoy it the most, right?

01:26:39.606 --> 01:26:42.931
I wanted to enjoy it the most
on my first play through.

01:26:42.931 --> 01:26:44.695
And sometimes I've had games where

01:26:44.695 --> 01:26:48.885
I load it up and I hit the
difficulty level selection

01:26:48.885 --> 01:26:51.925
and I'm just like, "(inhales)
I'm getting anxiety just now.

01:26:51.925 --> 01:26:53.154
(chuckles) I'm already getting anxiety.

01:26:53.154 --> 01:26:54.094
You know what?

01:26:54.094 --> 01:26:55.375
Maybe I'll play this
game another time, yeah."

01:26:55.375 --> 01:26:56.455
- This is why I like games that,

01:26:56.455 --> 01:26:57.555
even if they have difficulty options,

01:26:57.555 --> 01:26:59.014
they let you just change it on the fly.

01:26:59.014 --> 01:27:00.105
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah, I like that a lot.

01:27:00.105 --> 01:27:00.944
- And there's consequences for it.

01:27:00.944 --> 01:27:02.060
And it's like, "Alright, well,

01:27:02.060 --> 01:27:03.894
this section is kind of
bullshit, I'ma knock it down."

01:27:03.894 --> 01:27:04.727
- How do you feel about people

01:27:04.727 --> 01:27:07.644
who purposely select easy mode?

01:27:07.644 --> 01:27:08.926
- Well, it depends on the game.

01:27:08.926 --> 01:27:09.885
There's some games where I'm like,

01:27:09.885 --> 01:27:11.124
you're actually just not playing the game,

01:27:11.124 --> 01:27:13.525
if you've pick the easy one
'cause it's far too easy.

01:27:13.525 --> 01:27:15.257
- But, like, there's that whole stigma,

01:27:15.257 --> 01:27:16.535
I guess, like, connotation,

01:27:16.535 --> 01:27:18.514
that like, "Oh, you're not a real gamer

01:27:18.514 --> 01:27:19.644
if you're playing it on easy mode.

01:27:19.644 --> 01:27:20.477
Get good, scrub."

01:27:20.477 --> 01:27:21.704
Like levels of things, but like-

01:27:21.704 --> 01:27:24.195
- I mean, obviously if I was
there in the room with them,

01:27:24.195 --> 01:27:25.514
I'd be like, "I'm a strong little baby.

01:27:25.514 --> 01:27:27.194
I'm not gonna click normal?"
(Joey laughs)

01:27:27.194 --> 01:27:29.694
But, you know, on the podcast,

01:27:30.802 --> 01:27:32.525
and if a general audience asked me,

01:27:32.525 --> 01:27:33.358
I'd be like, "Yeah, of course,

01:27:33.358 --> 01:27:35.126
you can you pick whatever
difficulty you want."

01:27:35.126 --> 01:27:36.432
But obviously if you're my
mate, I'm gonna rinse you.

01:27:36.432 --> 01:27:38.884
- Play baby mode 'Mario Kart.'

01:27:38.884 --> 01:27:40.169
- I'm like, "Are you playing 'Mario Kart'

01:27:40.169 --> 01:27:41.123
with baby mode on?"

01:27:41.123 --> 01:27:42.347
No, you're not.
- No, you're not.

01:27:42.347 --> 01:27:44.079
No, no, no, no, no. (laughs)

01:27:44.079 --> 01:27:45.745
- No, no, no. Yeah, I mean,
it's different, right?

01:27:45.745 --> 01:27:47.041
Obviously you'll poke fun at your friends,

01:27:47.041 --> 01:27:48.145
you'll fuck around with it.
- Yeah, of course, of course.

01:27:48.145 --> 01:27:49.498
But obviously in general,

01:27:49.498 --> 01:27:50.618
I think that you can play

01:27:50.618 --> 01:27:51.785
whatever fucking difficulty you want.

01:27:51.785 --> 01:27:52.618
I don't give a fuck.

01:27:52.618 --> 01:27:53.730
Why would I care?

01:27:53.730 --> 01:27:54.804
What does it take away from me?

01:27:54.804 --> 01:27:55.637
- Just have fun.

01:27:55.637 --> 01:27:56.785
Just have fun with the game.
- Yeah, exactly.

01:27:56.785 --> 01:27:57.860
- If you wanna be a little baby bitch,

01:27:57.860 --> 01:27:59.017
you can be a little baby bitch.

01:27:59.017 --> 01:28:00.683
I don't care. You have
the right to do that.

01:28:00.683 --> 01:28:01.516
You paid the 60 bucks.

01:28:01.516 --> 01:28:02.555
- You have the right to be a baby bitch.

01:28:02.555 --> 01:28:04.926
- You paid the 60 bucks, you get to do it.

01:28:04.926 --> 01:28:07.771
I think it's good 'cause
not everyone, you know,

01:28:07.771 --> 01:28:09.075
obviously some people
have disabilities as well.

01:28:09.075 --> 01:28:10.673
They can't play the game
on the hardest difficulty

01:28:10.673 --> 01:28:11.882
'cause maybe they can't do it.

01:28:11.882 --> 01:28:14.723
You know, I just think
accessibility is good in gaming.

01:28:14.723 --> 01:28:16.981
I think that one of the things
that pisses me off most,

01:28:16.981 --> 01:28:19.152
and it's always the Japanese
game companies that do this,

01:28:19.152 --> 01:28:21.761
is it like the accessibility
options in their games

01:28:21.761 --> 01:28:22.594
are terrible.

01:28:22.594 --> 01:28:24.383
Like they don't let you change anything.

01:28:24.383 --> 01:28:26.341
No button remapping, none of that.

01:28:26.341 --> 01:28:28.611
I love it when games are like,
"Bro, what do you wanna do?

01:28:28.611 --> 01:28:30.951
How big do you want the
character models to be?

01:28:30.951 --> 01:28:31.921
No, not that, sorry.

01:28:31.921 --> 01:28:33.200
How bold do you want the outlines to be?

01:28:33.200 --> 01:28:34.791
- Do you ever use button remapping?

01:28:34.791 --> 01:28:36.440
- Yeah, all the time.
- Really?

01:28:36.440 --> 01:28:37.560
I've never used it.

01:28:37.560 --> 01:28:38.751
- I've never used it in my life.

01:28:38.751 --> 01:28:40.090
- I love button remapping.

01:28:40.090 --> 01:28:42.410
And it pisses me off that
a lot of games don't do it.

01:28:42.410 --> 01:28:43.479
And a lot of the indie devs

01:28:43.479 --> 01:28:44.720
are normally the ones who include

01:28:44.720 --> 01:28:46.138
a shit ton of accessibility options.

01:28:46.138 --> 01:28:48.042
- But that's a lot of PC games as well.

01:28:48.042 --> 01:28:50.837
Not a lot of console games
have button remapping, right?

01:28:50.837 --> 01:28:52.127
- Yeah, I mean, the
beauty of console games

01:28:52.127 --> 01:28:53.787
is that it's just plug and play.

01:28:53.787 --> 01:28:54.620
It's very simple.

01:28:54.620 --> 01:28:57.057
Just put a disc in or whatever,
or you download the game,

01:28:57.057 --> 01:28:58.297
and you just start playing.

01:28:58.297 --> 01:29:00.700
- Okay, so the argument
behind accessibility options

01:29:00.700 --> 01:29:03.059
and button remapping especially,

01:29:03.059 --> 01:29:03.961
especially with people who are,

01:29:03.961 --> 01:29:05.198
you know, maybe someone has a disability

01:29:05.198 --> 01:29:07.520
where they can't use one
of their hands properly

01:29:07.520 --> 01:29:09.780
and maybe there's a button
where they can't press jump,

01:29:09.780 --> 01:29:11.900
but they can press the jump
button with this finger.

01:29:11.900 --> 01:29:13.180
So the idea is that,

01:29:13.180 --> 01:29:15.999
even though, yes, this is
probably the best layout,

01:29:15.999 --> 01:29:18.478
someone out there might
have a way easier time

01:29:18.478 --> 01:29:20.491
with this button being on this one, right?

01:29:20.491 --> 01:29:21.792
So just give them the option to remap it.

01:29:21.792 --> 01:29:23.189
- No, no, no, yeah.
- Why wouldn't you?

01:29:23.189 --> 01:29:24.022
- Yeah.

01:29:24.022 --> 01:29:25.700
No, I'm definitely not
against button remapping,

01:29:25.700 --> 01:29:27.419
I've just personally never used it, yeah.

01:29:27.419 --> 01:29:29.300
- Yeah, Nintendo's gotten
a lot better at it as well,

01:29:29.300 --> 01:29:31.320
I think, actually, I think so.

01:29:31.320 --> 01:29:33.140
But they're awkward sometimes with it.

01:29:33.140 --> 01:29:35.115
And also colorblind options.

01:29:35.115 --> 01:29:37.979
"The Last of Us" had amazing
accessibility options.

01:29:37.979 --> 01:29:39.979
Like you could change it

01:29:39.979 --> 01:29:43.629
so everything in the
thing was just two colors.

01:29:43.629 --> 01:29:44.469
Like it's all gray

01:29:44.469 --> 01:29:46.739
and the models are just bright red

01:29:46.739 --> 01:29:47.715
and bright blue.
- Oh, that's cool.

01:29:47.715 --> 01:29:49.999
- So even someone who's
completely like, you know,

01:29:49.999 --> 01:29:52.979
has a really bad a case of
vision can play the game

01:29:52.979 --> 01:29:55.239
'cause they can see the
models' outlines and stuff.

01:29:55.239 --> 01:29:57.180
And then you can also just
turn stuff on for yourself,

01:29:57.180 --> 01:29:58.430
like if you prefer color...

01:29:58.430 --> 01:30:00.189
Like a lot of people play "Apex Legends"

01:30:00.189 --> 01:30:01.889
with the colorblind settings on

01:30:01.889 --> 01:30:03.589
to change the color of the bars and stuff

01:30:03.589 --> 01:30:06.328
to make it more visible, you know?

01:30:06.328 --> 01:30:07.579
I think that especially...

01:30:07.579 --> 01:30:09.506
Oh, another one. Okay, sorry,
I'm doing another rant now.

01:30:09.506 --> 01:30:12.592
This is one thing that I think
there's absolutely no excuse

01:30:12.592 --> 01:30:14.888
why there shouldn't be an option
on every single video game.

01:30:14.888 --> 01:30:15.840
Subtitles.

01:30:15.840 --> 01:30:18.277
Why is there not subtitles
on every single video game?

01:30:18.277 --> 01:30:19.289
They have the script.

01:30:19.289 --> 01:30:20.789
- Yeah, I hate it.

01:30:21.742 --> 01:30:22.575
- I agree with that.

01:30:22.575 --> 01:30:24.724
- I hate games that don't have subtitles.

01:30:24.724 --> 01:30:26.644
- Sometimes I don't wanna
have to listen to it

01:30:26.644 --> 01:30:27.483
at full volume,

01:30:27.483 --> 01:30:29.335
and sometimes maybe there's
explosions and shit going on,

01:30:29.335 --> 01:30:30.168
I want to read it.

01:30:30.168 --> 01:30:33.224
They have the script,
just plop that shit in.

01:30:33.224 --> 01:30:36.513
- It's just like, what is
it about, not just gaming,

01:30:36.513 --> 01:30:38.430
but movie audio mixing,

01:30:39.353 --> 01:30:40.534
especially if you're like...
- Oh yeah.

01:30:40.534 --> 01:30:42.224
- I remember I watched the
"Night Crawlers" yesterday

01:30:42.224 --> 01:30:47.224
with Sydney and, you know,
we watched a few movies.

01:30:47.284 --> 01:30:51.473
And we turned up the TV
to almost full volume.

01:30:51.473 --> 01:30:53.774
Character starts speaking, and
it was just like, (mumbles).

01:30:53.774 --> 01:30:54.893
(Joey laughs)

01:30:54.893 --> 01:30:56.313
I'm just like, "What?

01:30:56.313 --> 01:30:57.146
What?

01:30:57.146 --> 01:30:58.045
Is there a subtitle option?"

01:30:58.045 --> 01:30:59.354
And then we turn on the TV to full volume

01:30:59.354 --> 01:31:01.604
and it's still like, (mumbles).

01:31:01.604 --> 01:31:03.106
And suddenly, out of nowhere,

01:31:03.106 --> 01:31:04.523
boom, boom, boom.

01:31:06.244 --> 01:31:08.182
I'm getting earache right now.

01:31:08.182 --> 01:31:09.015
What the hell's going on?

01:31:09.015 --> 01:31:10.214
- I had some compression
on this shit, my god.

01:31:10.214 --> 01:31:11.574
- I literally had that happen to me

01:31:11.574 --> 01:31:13.443
when I watched "Interstellar" last week.

01:31:13.443 --> 01:31:15.112
(Connor laughing)
Like, oh my god,

01:31:15.112 --> 01:31:17.148
it's a fantastic movie,
don't get me wrong,

01:31:17.148 --> 01:31:18.387
and I love Matthew McConaughey,

01:31:18.387 --> 01:31:20.387
but, man, listening to him

01:31:20.387 --> 01:31:23.784
is like listening to a
subwoofer that barely works.

01:31:23.784 --> 01:31:24.844
This is like (imitates subwoofer).

01:31:24.844 --> 01:31:25.784
- 'Cause when they're mixing these movies,

01:31:25.784 --> 01:31:28.844
they're mixing them on these
gigantic audio editing suites

01:31:28.844 --> 01:31:29.844
where you can hear everything.

01:31:29.844 --> 01:31:32.682
And I'm like, "No, edit this
on a fucking ear port, bro,

01:31:32.682 --> 01:31:34.742
so you can hear what most
people are gonna listen to,

01:31:34.742 --> 01:31:36.092
like when they're listening to this."

01:31:36.092 --> 01:31:37.772
- I'm like, it's this
amazing scene, you know,

01:31:37.772 --> 01:31:39.091
when Matthew McConaughey is giving this

01:31:39.091 --> 01:31:41.284
really intense speech,

01:31:41.284 --> 01:31:44.441
and all I'm hearing is
just these fucking organs.

01:31:44.441 --> 01:31:45.663
And it's just like, "Ah."

01:31:45.663 --> 01:31:47.367
And Matthews like, (mumbles),

01:31:47.367 --> 01:31:49.960
Like, I don't know what
you're saying. (laughs)

01:31:49.960 --> 01:31:51.804
Speak up.
(Garnt and Connor laughing)

01:31:51.804 --> 01:31:52.841
- 'Cause I suppose some of the time,

01:31:52.841 --> 01:31:56.063
like the audio mixing
online video games as well,

01:31:56.063 --> 01:31:58.041
it's like watching a bass-boosted meme.

01:31:58.041 --> 01:31:59.291
(Connor and Joey laughing)

01:31:59.291 --> 01:32:02.804
You know, where the dialogue is so quiet

01:32:02.804 --> 01:32:04.801
and your ears just get fucking destroyed.

01:32:04.801 --> 01:32:05.821
(Joey growling)

01:32:05.821 --> 01:32:08.618
- Yeah, I fucking love YouTube
videos from small YouTubers

01:32:08.618 --> 01:32:10.594
whose audio is way too fucking quiet

01:32:10.594 --> 01:32:13.541
and the music is like, dun, dun, dun, dun,

01:32:13.541 --> 01:32:15.340
do, do, do, do, do,

01:32:15.340 --> 01:32:16.699
and you can't fucking hear them.

01:32:16.699 --> 01:32:19.348
I dunno why I love it.
- It's my favorite.

01:32:19.348 --> 01:32:21.593
- It's so charming.
- I know, it's so pure.

01:32:21.593 --> 01:32:22.489
I love it.

01:32:22.489 --> 01:32:23.750
- Yeah, subtitles on video games.

01:32:23.750 --> 01:32:25.667
This is why we need it,

01:32:26.515 --> 01:32:28.526
even in your own language, right?

01:32:28.526 --> 01:32:30.301
- Yeah, yeah, so there should
be absolutely no reason

01:32:30.301 --> 01:32:31.470
why there shouldn't be subtitles,

01:32:31.470 --> 01:32:33.409
'cause they have to write
the script for the game.

01:32:33.409 --> 01:32:34.491
Just put the fucking script

01:32:34.491 --> 01:32:35.787
into the software that can do this.

01:32:35.787 --> 01:32:38.469
Yeah, someone has to time
it, okay, that sucks, but-

01:32:38.469 --> 01:32:39.646
- And I hate how it's, like,

01:32:39.646 --> 01:32:43.258
a lot of games, the default is off.

01:32:43.258 --> 01:32:44.337
Just make it on,

01:32:44.337 --> 01:32:46.037
and if you don't like it,
then you can turn it off.

01:32:46.037 --> 01:32:47.857
- Also, I think a lot of
games as well do this,

01:32:47.857 --> 01:32:49.052
and I think every game should do this,

01:32:49.052 --> 01:32:51.795
is that they let you choose
how big you want the text,

01:32:51.795 --> 01:32:52.710
the color of the text,

01:32:52.710 --> 01:32:53.995
the outline of the text,
the shadow and stuff,

01:32:53.995 --> 01:32:55.682
so you can get the subtitles just right.

01:32:55.682 --> 01:32:56.763
So, you know, again,

01:32:56.763 --> 01:32:59.662
if you can't really see very
well, you know, you should...

01:32:59.662 --> 01:33:00.992
I don't understand why

01:33:00.992 --> 01:33:02.212
games don't just give
you all these options.

01:33:02.212 --> 01:33:03.852
I get it, it's a crunch,
they don't have time,

01:33:03.852 --> 01:33:04.892
but I mean, it's like, "Alright,

01:33:04.892 --> 01:33:06.877
well, just fuck the people
who can't play the game

01:33:06.877 --> 01:33:07.732
like everyone else, right?

01:33:07.732 --> 01:33:08.565
Just fuck them, right?

01:33:08.565 --> 01:33:09.842
Yeah, fuck them."

01:33:09.842 --> 01:33:13.022
Which is why everyone
loves to clown on Xbox,

01:33:13.022 --> 01:33:13.855
and I get it.

01:33:13.855 --> 01:33:16.886
You know, I'm an Xbox
boy myself, I love Xbox.

01:33:16.886 --> 01:33:19.878
I think Xbox have done some
of the most amazing things

01:33:19.878 --> 01:33:20.711
for accessibility.

01:33:20.711 --> 01:33:24.377
Have you seen the controller they've made?

01:33:24.377 --> 01:33:25.646
It's like this pad, right,

01:33:25.646 --> 01:33:27.712
and you can literally
hook anything up to it,

01:33:27.712 --> 01:33:29.722
literally anything into a controller.

01:33:29.722 --> 01:33:30.555
And it's set up

01:33:30.555 --> 01:33:32.835
so that you can just turn
anything into a controller

01:33:32.835 --> 01:33:34.901
so that no matter how your position is

